<mxCell id="n254" value="External — owned by PP (cross-schema, real FK)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#12181F;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="72" y="1391" width="600" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n255" value="FK* on users.id / HCM.shift_assignments / INVENTORY.products|warehouses|stock_batches|stock_serials references core or other-Core-module tables outside the MES schema. INVENTORY/users references are REAL cross-schema FKs (Inventory is present on every plan; users is Laravel’s own core table) but are read via InventoryService in application code, never a raw join, per CLAUDE.md §2 module-boundary discipline. HCM.shift_assignments is informational only (HCM is plan-optional relative to MES). PP.pp_boms/PP.pp_recipes are REAL cross-schema FKs (PP is sequenced immediately before MES in CLAUDE.md §5 and is a hard dependency for material composition) but MES’s own application code reads them via PpService::getActiveBom/getActiveRecipe/scaleRecipe, never a raw join — see MES_SPECS.md §3B/§5. mes_prod_events and mes_audit_logs are append-only (no UPDATE/DELETE in application code). CHECK constraints (not modeled as separate cells) restrict enum-like columns to the fixed value sets in MES_SPECS.md §3." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1440" width="2460" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
